00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.161
<v Maya>That's a great way to put it.</v>

43
00:05:12.761 --> 00:05:17.564
<v Daniel>But, I mean, why would that even change the meal? You already had the ingredients. You already knew they were on the counter.</v>

44
00:05:18.195 --> 00:05:33.083
<v Maya>Well, what's fascinating here is that your sous chef analogy isolates exactly why this study design is so vital. It has a very specific behavioral mechanism, like does synthesizing existing data and slapping a clear label on it alter</v>

45
00:05:33.123 --> 00:05:34.704
<v Maya>human attention and human action?</v>

46
00:05:35.044 --> 00:05:35.225
<v Daniel>Right.</v>

47
00:05:35.805 --> 00:05:39.327
<v Maya>If the machine isn't giving you new facts, does it still change what you do?</v>

48
00:05:39.747 --> 00:05:46.691
