50
00:05:56.882 --> 00:05:59.643
<v Daniel>Okay, and to translate that into real-world impact?</v>

51
00:06:00.243 --> 00:06:06.566
<v Maya>That is a 1.2 percentage point increase on a control rate of 1.3%. You're</v>

52
00:06:06.987 --> 00:06:08.327
<v Daniel>saying placements nearly doubled.</v>

53
00:06:08.728 --> 00:06:09.408
<v Maya>Essentially, yes.</v>

54
00:06:09.971 --> 00:06:17.398
<v Daniel>Just because a risk score was made visible on a screen, the human authorities were twice as likely to remove a child from a home. I mean, that sounds incredibly aggressive.</v>

55
00:06:17.678 --> 00:06:26.867
<v Maya>It sounds aggressive until you look at exactly where those interventions happened. The effect was intensely concentrated in the specific group the machine flagged as very high risk.</v>

56
