<v Daniel>They can't tell which one it is.</v>

86
00:10:29.819 --> 00:10:44.563
<v Maya>No, the researchers cannot tell us whether the score mathematically improved the human's beliefs, whether it simply directed their scarce attention to a file they might have skimmed, or whether it gave them the institutional cover to act on existing concerns. It could</v>

87
00:10:44.623 --> 00:10:46.043
<v Maya>easily be a combination of all three.</v>

88
00:10:46.822 --> 00:11:01.341
<v Daniel>Okay, but let's play devil's advocate again. This sounds almost too perfectly effective. What's the catch? Because the sample size of 34 investigators in a single county feels like a tiny foundation to build our entire philosophy of human-AI</v>

89
00:11:01.381 --> 00:11:02.002
<v Daniel>partnership on.</v>

90
00:11:02.435 --> 00:11:16.926
<v Maya>We definitely need to be honest about the limits of this single study. First, as you noted, this is only one county in Pennsylvania. Right. What works there might not map perfectly onto a massive urban center like New York or Los Angeles. Second,</v>

91
