<v Maya>downstream. Humans respond to what they receive. The algorithm, being purely mathematical, sends the field investigators a totally different, riskier pool of cases than they are used to seeing. I see. But the investigators are human, right? They</v>

125
00:15:40.758 --> 00:15:54.344
<v Maya>rely heavily on their own prior history and experience, which the algorithm weighs differently. They look at these new algorithmically flagged families, think this doesn't fit my traditional profile of danger, and they choose not to open cases for them.</v>

126
00:15:55.172 --> 00:15:59.494
